    {
      "kind": "equations",
      "title": "Variational Monte Carlo",
      "lines": [
        "$E_\\theta=\\sum_{\\mathbf{n}\\in\\mathcal{H}_N}P_{\\theta,N}(\\mathbf{n})E_{\\rm loc}(\\mathbf{n})$",
        "$E_{\\rm loc}(\\mathbf{n})=\\sum_{\\mathbf{n}\\prime}H_{\\mathbf{n},\\mathbf{n}\\prime}\\,\\frac{\\Psi_\\theta(\\mathbf{n}\\prime)}{\\Psi_\\theta(\\mathbf{n})}$",
        "$\\nabla_\\theta E=2\\langle(E_{\\rm loc}-\\overline{E})\\,\\nabla_\\theta\\log\\Psi_\\theta\\rangle$",
        "Equilibrate fresh walkers before updates; assess frozen checkpoints."
      ],
      "fontsize": 44,
      "step": 0.15,
      "footer": "Retained configurations are correlated. Proposal spacing, burn-in, independent evaluation chains and time-block statistics are recorded."
    },
    {
      "kind": "equations",
      "title": "Stochastic reconfiguration",
      "lines": [
        "$O_k=\\partial_{\\theta_k}\\log\\Psi_\\theta,\\quad S_{kl}=\\langle(O_k-\\overline{O}_k)(O_l-\\overline{O}_l)\\rangle$",
        "$f_k=\\langle(O_k-\\overline{O}_k)(E_{\\rm loc}-\\overline{E})\\rangle$",
        "$\\Delta\\boldsymbol{\\theta}=-\\eta\\,(S+\\tau I)^{-1}\\mathbf{f}$",
        "VMC: SR direction applied with native SGD; no Adam on top."
      ],
      "fontsize": 42,
      "step": 0.16,
      "footer": "S is the log-derivative covariance / quantum metric, not generally the energy Hessian. Learning rate absorbs the conventional factor of two."
